---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faq = [{ question: 'Why does a browser need a button press?', answer: 'Browsers commonly expose a connected gamepad after the user interacts with it. Press a face button or move a stick after connecting.' }, { question: 'Should I close Steam?', answer: 'Steam Input and other controller tools can change mappings or hold the device. Close them temporarily when diagnosing a browser detection issue.' }];
---
<BaseLayout title="Gamepad Tester Not Detecting Controller – USB & Bluetooth Fixes" description="Is your gamepad tester not detecting a controller? Connect it in Windows, macOS or Linux first, then try practical fixes for USB, Bluetooth, browser focus, Steam Input and driver mappings." faqs={faq}><section class="article-hero"><div class="shell article-hero-inner"><span class="subpage-kicker">TROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE</span><h1>Controller not detected?<br /><span>Start here.</span></h1><p class="lede">A practical checklist for Xbox, PlayStation, Switch and generic controllers that do not appear in a browser-based gamepad tester.</p></div></section><section class="guide-grid shell"><article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">QUICK FIXES</span><h2>Try these in order</h2><ol><li>Connect or pair the controller in your operating system before opening the tester.</li><li>Press any face button or move a stick.</li><li>Try a different USB cable or port.</li><li>Close Steam, browser games and controller remappers.</li><li>Reload the page in desktop Chrome or Edge.</li><li>Pair Bluetooth again and check system settings.</li></ol></article><article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">WHAT THE PAGE CAN READ</span><h2>Browser limits</h2><p>The tester can only display data that the operating system exposes through the standard Gamepad API. A controller can work in a console or native game while remaining invisible to a browser.</p><ul><li>This page cannot pair Bluetooth or install USB drivers.</li><li>Some browsers require user interaction first.</li><li>Vibration support is separate from button detection.</li><li>Driver and Steam mappings can change button labels.</li></ul></article></section><section class="faq-section shell"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">DETECTION FAQ</span><h2>Still stuck?</h2></div></div><div class="faq-grid">{faq.map((item, index) => <details open={index === 0}><summary>{item.question}<span>+</span></summary><p>{item.answer}</p></details>)}</div></section></BaseLayout>
